sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Brodland (2002) / Krieg et al. (2008) / Maître et al. (2012) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) and zebrafish germ-layer cortical tension sorting, with time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling (Pass 3) faithfully reproduces Danio rerio (zebrafish shield-stage gastrula germ-layer progenitors: ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio rerio (zebrafish shield-stage gastrula germ-layer progenitors: ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8beed34/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8beed34/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py; output: docs/media/differential_interfacial_tension_sorting_comparison.png; organism: Danio rerio (zebrafish shield-stage gastrula germ-layer progenitors: ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8beed34; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 04e6692e5c44347cdef3ff055c0cf966e6a50c079cad3d06d965f070f3683587; artifact_sha256: 5ffd7144ad26d4d8b06fe5b2d7ddf385312e2ed564432552abf59cecd5490808; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Brodland (2002) J. Biomech. Eng. Eqs. 1-4: Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) decomposing cell-cell interfacial tension into actomyosin cortical tension minus cadherin adhesion (gamma_{alpha,beta} = beta_alpha + beta_beta - omega_{alpha,beta}). | Krieg et al. (2008) Nature Cell Biology Figs. 1-4: AFM cortical tension hierarchy across zebrafish shield-stage germ-layer progenitors (beta_ectoderm ~ 50 < beta_mesoderm ~ 95 < beta_endoderm ~ 130 pN/um) obtained by lefty1 / cyclops / cyclops+casanova mRNA injection, concentric 3-germ-layer sorting, Blebbistatin Myosin-II inhibition arrest, and caMLCK ectodermal cortical stiffening sorting reversal. | Maître et al. (2012) Science Eq. 1: Young-Dupré cell-doublet contact angle cos(theta) = 1 - gamma_cc/(2*gamma_cm) and normalized contact radius r_c/R = sin(theta). | Chen & Schier (2001), Dubrulle et al. (2015), van Boxtel et al. (2015), Hagos & Dougan (2007): Nodal (Squint/Cyclops) acts as a graded marginal morphogen whose signalling domain is set by a temporal window between sphere and shield stage and whose dose specifies mesoderm vs endoderm; Gritsman et al. (1999): MZoep embryos lack all mesendoderm.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D deformable DITH cell sorting across all 4 perturbation regimes (wild-type engulfment, caMLCK cortex reversal, Blebbistatin Myosin-II inhibition, and high-HIT mushroom doublet) plus simultaneous 3-germ-layer concentric stratification (r_E = 0.870 > r_M = 0.663 > r_N = 0.446), a 7-point continuous beta_E sweep across the sorting inversion threshold beta_E = beta_M = 95 pN/um, and the Young-Dupré doublet contact curve. | Pass 3: a reduced time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling — 1D marginal Nodal field C(x,t) with range lambda = 3 tiers and rise time tau_N = 0.6 h from 4.0 hpf, two-threshold Hill dose -> cortical tension target (beta_E/beta_M/beta_N = 50/95/130 pN/um), first-order cortex relaxation tau_beta = 0.5 h, and a continuous-cortex DITH closure gamma_ij = (2/3)|beta_i - beta_j| re-evaluated every MCS inside the lattice sorter; the model reproduces 5 mesendoderm / 2 endoderm tiers at shield stage, establishes the Krieg hierarchy by 4.87 hpf, reaches Delta_r = +0.350 at 7 hpf, and gives Delta_r = 0 with no mesendoderm in the Nodal-null (C0 = 0) control; 5-point C0 dose sweep. | Computer-vision segmentation of a zebrafish blastoderm transplantation GFP/RFP micrograph (`germ_layer_doublet_specimen.jpg`) across both layered engulfment (Row B, radial profile r = 0.9301, RMSE = 0.1844) and the protruding mushroom doublet (Row C, empirical r_c/R = 0.9717).; transfer_boundary: 2D lattice DITH representation of 3D zebrafish germ-layer progenitor reaggregates and blastoderm transplants; the circular 60-cell disc with medium all round is a reaggregate, not an embryo, so 'internalization' is sorting toward the disc centre. | The Nodal coupling is 1D in tier distance from the margin, each cell's Nodal exposure is frozen to its tier of origin (specification memory), there is no epiboly / YSL motion and no Lefty feedback; lambda, K_M, K_N, tau_N and tau_beta were chosen to reproduce recalled literature anchors (~5 mesendoderm tiers, endoderm from tiers 1-2), not fitted to a digitised pSmad2 profile. | The vendored specimen is a Wikimedia whole-blastoderm / yolk-cell transplant micrograph, not a Krieg et al. (2008) progenitor aggregate or a shield-stage internalization image; it is a proxy for layered GFP/RFP sorting, and no specimen underlies the Nodal row of the figure.; does_not_claim: Does not model sub-second single-molecule E-cadherin bond rupture kinetics, whole-embryo epiboly yolk-syncytial-layer microtubule pulling, 2D/3D Nodal-Lefty reaction-diffusion, or quantitative pSmad2 gradient fits.]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/aja.1002030302>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)80720-5>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2015.09.014>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/35079121>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1705>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-017-00146-x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0704252104>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.1449491>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1225399>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-7-22>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.126.4.827>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.05042> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.892"^^xsd:double .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8beed34/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "8beed34" .
}

